{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Cm4Gz6vqnYfqwF5d8ZSXn","type":"tool_result","content":"160\t  - **`prd.json` lies about US-044 (PythonPlot) and US-050 (Image) — both marked `passes: true`, neither is actually in the registry or schema discriminated union.** Cross-checked: `src/widgets/registry.ts` `WidgetType` union has 13 types but excludes `pythonPlot` and `image`; `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` discriminated union likewise excludes them. The US-051 learning note flagged Image; PythonPlot has the same fate. Test plan needed to acknowledge this honestly without dropping the AC-mandated coverage — solution was to keep §3.4.8 / §3.4.14 sections complete with their pass criteria but front-load a **NOTE** at the bottom + a Known-Limitations item §4.6 with a one-line `grep` to verify.\n161\t  - **Test plans should reference all the seed-test courses already in `/courses/`** — `pexp-test`, `cloze-test`, `dragmatch-test`, `datatable-test`, `video-test` cover the widgets that don't fit naturally into the seed `gauss-basics` course. Calling these out per-widget gives the reviewer a fast path even if they skip §2's \"Test Courses to Generate\" step (which requires a full ralph chain run).\n162\t  - **Time-budget signal in the document.** AC says ≤30/≤60 min targets — the way I made this realistic was: (a) §2 explicitly tells reviewers they can skip course generation and use seeds (saves ~30 min × 3 courses), (b) §3 sections are ordered so the reviewer can do dashboard → wizard → seed-lesson nav → widgets → chat → theme → sources → schema → header in roughly that flow without backtracking, (c) widget §3.4 sub-sections are short enough (5–10 boxes each) that the whole §3.4 is ~10 minutes if no failures.\n163\t  - **`courses/` already has six dedicated widget-test courses.** `ls courses/` showed cloze-test, datatable-test, dragmatch-test, gauss-basics, pexp-test, video-test — handy reference for any future story that needs a minimal repro lesson for a specific widget without spinning up the wizard.\n164\t  - **The keyboard shortcut list in `src/components/ShortcutsModal.tsx` is the canonical source of truth** for what keys are wired. AC mentions j/k/⌘B/⌘. but ShortcutsModal.tsx also exposes Space (mark current section), n (next lesson), p (previous lesson), f (focus mode), and arrow keys ↑/↓ as aliases for k/j. Test plan covers j/k/⌘B/⌘. + Reset session per AC; the others aren't mandated so I didn't bloat the checklist.\n165\t  - **Authoring tip: pick widget pass criteria from the original AC string.** Each `US-NNN` AC in `prd.json` has phrases like \"button morphs to **Stop** with `--danger` styling\", \"**Page X of Y** indicator centered below table\", \"italic suffix `— stopped by user` renders on its own line\". Quoting these verbatim in the checkbox items both (a) anchors the criterion to the originating story and (b) means a future reviewer can `git blame`/grep back to the spec source if a behavior changes.\n166\t---\n167\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a67c3911-b062-408c-adef-83e9de9f7090","uuid":"c5c8b492-3088-40c7-9f58-1b5e40c45682","timestamp":"2026-05-04T07:54:24.341Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-057/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","content":"  - **`prd.json` lies about US-044 (PythonPlot) and US-050 (Image) — both marked `passes: true`, neither is actually in the registry or schema discriminated union.** Cross-checked: `src/widgets/registry.ts` `WidgetType` union has 13 types but excludes `pythonPlot` and `image`; `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` discriminated union likewise excludes them. The US-051 learning note flagged Image; PythonPlot has the same fate. Test plan needed to acknowledge this honestly without dropping the AC-mandated coverage — solution was to keep §3.4.8 / §3.4.14 sections complete with their pass criteria but front-load a **NOTE** at the bottom + a Known-Limitations item §4.6 with a one