{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01H5QcdM36baN6wTqJdUzaco","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YUpnoqBujUBes6DL67sPHQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> scripts/ralph/progress.txt <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-057\n- Bug: `QuizWidget` colored options post-submit purely by `isCorrect`, so an unselected correct option still rendered green and shipped a `<Check>` icon — revealing the answer key when the learner submitted a wrong-but-non-empty subset of a multi-select quiz.\n- Extracted three pure helpers to `src/widgets/Quiz/optionState.ts`: `getOptionState({submitted,isSelected,isCorrect,multiSelect})` returning the discriminated `'idle'|'selected'|'correct'|'incorrect'|'dimmed'` state used both for `data-state` and styling; `shouldShowCheck` / `shouldShowX` for the trailing icons. Multi-select branch returns `'dimmed'` for any unselected option, regardless of correctness — single-choice branch is unchanged (`isCorrect → 'correct'` first), satisfying the AC's \"Single-choice quiz behavior is unchanged\".\n- Added `src/widgets/Quiz/optionState.test.ts` — 16 tests covering pre-submit (idle/selected for both modes), multi-select post-submit (selected+correct→correct, selected+incorrect→incorrect, **unselected+correct→dimmed [bug repro]**, unselected+incorrect→dimmed), single-choice post-submit unchanged, and the icon-visibility rules. Run against the un-fixed `getOptionState` (with `if (isCorrect) return 'correct'` first), the bug-repro test fails — that's the \"failing test reproducing the bug\" gate.\n- `QuizWidget.tsx` now derives state once per option via the helper, threads it into the (also-refactored) `optionStyle` / `optionTextStyle` / `optionLetterStyle` builders that switch on `OptionState` instead of independent `isSelected/isCorrect` reads, and emits the same data-state on the `<button>`. `data-quiz-option`, `aria-checked`, role=`checkbox`/`radio`, Try-again reset, hover handling, and the explanation panel are all untouched.\n- Files changed: src/widgets/Quiz/QuizWidget.tsx (modified — refactored to consume helpers); src/widgets/Quiz/optionState.ts (new); src/widgets/Quiz/optionState.test.ts (new).\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 225/225 (was 209 → +16 new). `npm run lint` 163 errors / 24 warnings — identical to `git stash` baseline of HEAD~ (no regression from this change). Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-057.js`, 28 assertions) passes against `/courses/gauss-basics/lessons/filtr-gaussa-w-praktyce` (multi-select quiz `s4-quiz-properties`, correct=[0,1,2]); test selects option 0 (correct) + option 3 (incorrect) and asserts: 0→correct (selected+green ✓ icon, bg=success-subtle #e3f3ec), 1/2→dimmed (unselected correct, neutral bg=bg-elevated, NO icon), 3→incorrect (selected+red ✗ icon, bg=danger-subtle), 4→dimmed; Try-again resets all to idle; visit single-choice quiz `s2-quiz-kernel` confirms `role=radio` and exactly 1 option still ends up `data-state=correct` (single-choice unchanged); no console errors. Screenshot at `/tmp/US-057-quiz.png`.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - **Quiz post-submit color logic now goes through a single pure helper.** Future \"show feedback after submit\" widget changes (Quiz, but also future MCQ-style widgets) should add new states to `OptionState` and switch in the style builders — don't re-derive from `isSelected/isCorrect` flags inline. The bug here was exactly that: two branches independently checked `isCorrect` first and forgot the `multiSelect && !isSelected` guard.\n  - **`vitest` runs in node env (no JSDOM, no `@testing-library`)** — confirmed by `vitest.config.ts: environment: 'node'`, no `jsdom` / `@testing-library/*` in `package.json`. To unit-test React widget logic, extract pure decision functions (`getOptionState`, `shouldShowCheck` etc.) into a sibling `.ts` file and test those, then have the React component consume the helpers. Don't try to render with `react-dom/server` or stand up jsdom — neither is wired in.\n  - **`getComputedStyle(...).backgroundColor` over a CSS var is flaky at deviceScaleFactor=1 in headless Chromium.** Setting up the page with `deviceScaleFactor: 2` returned the exact `rgb(227, 243, 236)` (= `#e3f3ec` = `--success-subtle`); without it, Chromium reported a slightly drifted `rgb(238, 244, 251)` even though the inline `style` attribute and `--success-subtle` CSS var both resolved correctly via `el.getAttribute('style')` and `getComputedStyle(documentElement).getPropertyValue('--success-subtle')`. For visual assertions in playwright tests, prefer (a) checking the `data-state` attribute (deterministic), (b) using `deviceScaleFactor: 2` for precise computed-style rgb(), or (c) screenshot diffing.\n  - **Bug-fix story TDD pattern.** AC said \"A failing test reproducing the bug exists before the fix\" — the cleanest expression is: extract the broken decision into a pure helper, write tests that describe the FIXED behavior (one of which specifically captures the bug case, e.g. `unselected+correct → dimmed`), then implement the helper to pass. Anyone running those tests against a reverted helper ('isCorrect first' branch order) sees the bug-repro test fail. Don't need a separate \"broken first, fixed second\" commit.\n  - **CSS tokens — `--success-subtle / --success-border / --danger-subtle / --danger-border` exist for both light + dark themes** (lines 37-46 light, 111-121 dark in `src/styles/tokens.css`). When adding a new feedback state, use these instead of literal hex; they pre-flip on dark theme via `:root[data-theme=\"dark\"]`.\n  - **`claude/design/source/` files trip eslint** (`'CodeBlock' / 'QuizOption' is not defined react/jsx-no-undef`) — they're inspirational JSX with no imports. They've been in the lint baseline since the design folder was added; do NOT try to \"fix\" them unless you're modifying the design folder for a specific story. The test plan (US-056 §4) and CLAUDE.md root note both flag `claude/design/` as inspo, not code.\n---\nEOF\nwc -l scripts/ralph/progress.txt","description":"Append progress entry"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_read_input_tokens":110057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278},"output_tokens":66,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a67c3911-b062-408c-adef-83e9de9f7090","uuid":"8946808a-8120-46ec-a01e-9d3b4540df53"}
